TAKEAWAYS
=========
1. The exact side hinge [21,24] is structurally special but polynomially reducible (L=4).
2. The strongest prime-length/irreducibility lane in the scanned window is the whole-equation Pell family:
   it contributes 4 prime lengths among its first 8 rows, including L=5 and L=29 with base-2 Cohn primes.
3. Exactness and irreducibility pull in different directions:
   the A_R hinge families maximize support/exactness, while the whole-equation family wins prime-length supply.
4. The family tournament is genuinely nontransitive
   (6 directed 3-cycles, SCC sizes [7,1,1]), and prime-length data flips 8 edges
   relative to the support/exactness-only ranking, so the polynomial carrier is not cosmetic.

ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
====================
Alternate vertices considered: raw intervals, lengths only, Pell equations,
coefficient rows, primes, Mersenne exponents, and proof obligations.
Chosen vertices: overlap-family carriers, because they preserve both the
interval containment predicate and the irreducible-polynomial bridge R_L(x).
Destroyed data: exact interval position beyond the shift x^a, asymptotic prime
production, and any support channel not visible from the block length.
